Package: epiLabR
Type: Package
Title: Educational Framework for Compartmental Epidemiological Modelling
Version: 0.3.0
Author: Vicente Castellar [aut, cre]
Authors@R: 
    person("Vicente", "Castellar",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "vic.sebastia@gmail.com")
Description: Tools for simulation and analysis of deterministic
    compartmental epidemiological models defined by systems of ordinary
    differential equations (ODEs). The package allows users to define
    custom epidemic models, simulate state trajectories over time, and
    explore model behaviour under different parameter settings. It
    includes implementations of classical models such as the
    susceptible-infectious (SI), susceptible-infectious-recovered (SIR),
    SIR with vital dynamics, susceptible-infectious-recovered-
    susceptible (SIRS), susceptible-exposed-infectious-recovered (SEIR),
    and susceptible-exposed-infectious-recovered-susceptible (SEIRS)
    models. An optional 'shiny' application is provided for interactive
    visualisation and exploration of epidemic scenarios. The
    methodological framework is based on Kermack and McKendrick (1927)
    <doi:10.1098/rspa.1927.0118>, Hethcote (2000)
    <doi:10.1137/S0036144500371907>, Soetaert et al. (2010)
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v033.i09>, and Ma (2020)
    <doi:10.1016/j.idm.2019.12.009>.
